## Scope — a slice #<%= parent %> does not name

**#<%= parent %>'s slicing plan has 37 `TimeForm` variants and 221 EN rules, but <%= slice.rules.size %> of those rules construct no `TimeForm` at all.** They clone an existing `TimeData` and mutate its attribute fields. They have no variant to be sliced by, so without this issue they would be orphaned — every one of the 37 variant slices would either skip them or all reach for them at once.

These rules own the `TimeData` attribute fields rather than the `form` field:

| Attribute | What sets it |
|---|---|
| `latent` | almost every rule here — promoting a latent token to a real one |
| `early_late` | `late/early/mid <time>`, `part of <named-month>` |
| `open_interval_direction` | `until <time>`, `from\|since\|after <time>`, `after <part-of-day>` |
| `timezone` | `<time> timezone`, `<time> (timezone)` |
| `direction` | `this past weekend`, `last <time>`, `next <time>`, `<time> before last\|after next` |

Those fields are declared on `TimeData` in `src/dimensions/time/mod.rs` and are therefore **#<%= spine_issue %> output** — this slice mutates them, it does not define them. A missing field is a spine follow-up, not an edit here.

